    "Description": "The podman tool manages pods, container images, and containers. It is part of the libpod library, which is for applications that use container pods. Container pods is a concept in Kubernetes.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* podman: podman: Quadlet install --replace non-truncating write retains removed host-access directives (CVE-2026-19730)\n\n* net/http: golang: Go net/http: Unencrypted HTTP/2 connections vulnerable to Denial of Service (CVE-2026-56853)\n\n* github.com/moby/go-archive: moby/go-archive: Arbitrary file write via link following in tar extraction (CVE-2026-17106)\n\n* podman: podman: The `podman run` command can be instructed to disable almost all sandboxing - including user-requested sandboxing - by image annotation (CVE-2026-94603)\n\n* net/http: golang: golang: Denial of Service via crafted HTTP Range headers (CVE-2026-78667)\n\n* crypto/tls: golang: crypto/tls: Denial of Service via multiple ECH outer extension references (CVE-2026-97031)\n\n* crypto/x509: golang: crypto/x509: Man-in-the-middle attacks via untrusted intermediate certificates (CVE-2026-111943)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
